(557050, 56660, 9073, '<td valign="top">Nice use of white balance to allow the filtered colour to  come through. I''m not sure about the application, though. The blue works very well - cold and threatening (a star filter would have made the hotspot sparkle). The red, though, is less menacing than simply warm. The other way around might have worked better for me. 6</td>', 'Nice use of white balance to allow the filtered colour to  come through. I''m not sure about the application, though. The blue works very well - cold and threatening (a star filter would have made the hotspot sparkle). The red, though, is less menacing than simply warm. The other way around might have worked better for me. 6', '2004-01-26 02:35:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(557052, 56465, 8054, '<td valign="top">Well exposed with good contrast. Very low noise considering the light levels. I''m not sure what pattern the light is intended to create other than to illuminate the subject''s face. The only problem I have with the light pattern is it is a little jittery.I think this type of shot would benefit from a smoother movement of the light source.</td>', 'Well exposed with good contrast. Very low noise considering the light levels. I''m not sure what pattern the light is intended to create other than to illuminate the subject''s face. The only problem I have with the light pattern is it is a little jittery.I think this type of shot would benefit from a smoother movement of the light source.', '2004-01-26 02:36:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(557058, 55912, 8054, '<td valign="top">Excellent interpretation of the challenge! Personally, with such a stark contrast between the black background and the border, I would have used a thinner frame instead to keep focus on the subject vs the frame. That is a minor fault but I still find this an excellent entry. I''m even willing to ignore the minor compression problem in the middle of the "paint stroke" 10!</td>', 'Excellent interpretation of the challenge! Personally, with such a stark contrast between the black background and the border, I would have used a thinner frame instead to keep focus on the subject vs the frame. That is a minor fault but I still find this an excellent entry. I''m even willing to ignore the minor compression problem in the middle of the "paint stroke" 10!', '2004-01-26 02:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(557064, 56982, 8054, '<td valign="top">Great photo and composure are marred by excessive compression and I understand the shot was taken at low light levels (as are most if not all).</td>', 'Great photo and composure are marred by excessive compression and I understand the shot was taken at low light levels (as are most if not all).', '2004-01-26 02:42:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(557066, 57050, 10170, '<td valign="top">Very effective</td>', 'Very effective', '2004-01-26 02:43:57.000000', NULL, 1),
