(558507, 56921, 327, '<td valign="top">Cute idea, reminds me of E.T. in the closet. :)</td>', 'Cute idea, reminds me of E.T. in the closet. :)', '2004-01-26 23:14:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(558509, 56549, 16352, '<td valign="top">Starlight filters rarely work - but this one really has - I love it - 3 seperate images from 1 image. It has really worked. My only concern is, as you may have guessed from the amount of discussion on the forum re "painting with light" is whether it is painting with light.<br/>Having been lucky enough to judge what is now a few hundred competitions in the last 30 years I feel I should say the first thing that happens is that they are sorted and any that do not immediatly seem to fit the category are dumped (hard but a fact). This is why so many competitions also run an "open category".  Your picture, as impressive as it is, would, I feel have been rejected at this stage. "Painting with Light" has a fairly tight definition in photography but still allows a lot of lattitude for creativity. <br/>I suspect that your scores may not reflect what the picture is worth which is a great shame. I believe if I was judging in another category I would have gone for an 8 possibly a 9 because you have managed to get those highlights working so well. <br/>I do hope you understand my reasons for marking it down<br/>David<br/></td>', 'Starlight filters rarely work - but this one really has - I love it - 3 seperate images from 1 image. It has really worked. My only concern is, as you may have guessed from the amount of discussion on the forum re "painting with light" is whether it is painting with light.Having been lucky enough to judge what is now a few hundred competitions in the last 30 years I feel I should say the first thing that happens is that they are sorted and any that do not immediatly seem to fit the category are dumped (hard but a fact). This is why so many competitions also run an "open category".  Your picture, as impressive as it is, would, I feel have been rejected at this stage. "Painting with Light" has a fairly tight definition in photography but still allows a lot of lattitude for creativity. I suspect that your scores may not reflect what the picture is worth which is a great shame. I believe if I was judging in another category I would have gone for an 8 possibly a 9 because you have managed to get those highlights working so well. I do hope you understand my reasons for marking it downDavid', '2004-01-26 23:14:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(558510, 56643, 327, '<td valign="top">I like the colors and the idea. I do think the dust and light flashes are a too distracting.</td>', 'I like the colors and the idea. I do think the dust and light flashes are a too distracting.', '2004-01-26 23:14:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(558511, 56220, 327, '<td valign="top">Pretty flowers and nice composition. The focus is soft but otherwise okay.</td>', 'Pretty flowers and nice composition. The focus is soft but otherwise okay.', '2004-01-26 23:15:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(558512, 56735, 10768, '<td valign="top">Very cool.  I''m anxious to see what this is.  I like the different colors and the repeated wavy lines throughout this photo.</td>', 'Very cool.  I''m anxious to see what this is.  I like the different colors and the repeated wavy lines throughout this photo.', '2004-01-26 23:15:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(558513, 56415, 9073, '<td valign="top">It''s during the voting when I see realisations of the challenge theme that I never would have thought about. Thank you. The water drops work beautifully with the light source. Lovely stuff. 8</td>', 'It''s during the voting when I see realisations of the challenge theme that I never would have thought about. Thank you. The water drops work beautifully with the light source. Lovely stuff. 8', '2004-01-26 23:16:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(558514, 57033, 10768, '<td valign="top">I''m anxious to see how this one was done.  Pretty cool!</td>', 'I''m anxious to see how this one was done.  Pretty cool!', '2004-01-26 23:17:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(558517, 57033, 3102, '<td valign="top">Finally!  A shot that seems to have met the challenge, AND in a creative way!  The description of the challenge specifically said to use a non-stationery light source, and practically nobody followed that requirement.  And those who DID follow it haven''t done nearly the job you have done here, in my opinion.  Congrats on an awesome, awesome shot.  I hope very much to see this wearing a blue ribbon next week!  - 10<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-02-02 19:54:22.</i></td>', 'Finally!  A shot that seems to have met the challenge, AND in a creative way!  The description of the challenge specifically said to use a non-stationery light source, and practically nobody followed that requirement.  And those who DID follow it haven''t done nearly the job you have done here, in my opinion.  Congrats on an awesome, awesome shot.  I hope very much to see this wearing a blue ribbon next week!  - 10', '2004-01-26 23:20:27.000000', '2004-02-02 19:54:22.000000', 1),
(558519, 57027, 16352, '<td valign="top">One of the few who seem to be genuinely painting with light according to the photographic definition. Makes me think very much of "Australian Aboriginal Dreamtime".<br/>Unfortunately I suspect it is likely to be hammered by non-photographers and anyone not understanding "painting with light"<br/>I think it''s great though.</td>', 'One of the few who seem to be genuinely painting with light according to the photographic definition. Makes me think very much of "Australian Aboriginal Dreamtime".Unfortunately I suspect it is likely to be hammered by non-photographers and anyone not understanding "painting with light"I think it''s great though.', '2004-01-26 23:21:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(558521, 56772, 16352, '<td valign="top">So there really are some who have entered who<br/>a: read the category description<br/>b: Understood it<br/>This is painting with light. Unfortunatly I think this (and a few others) will be hammered by non-photographers and photographers who misunderstand the photographic definition of painting with light. Well done.<br/></td>', 'So there really are some who have entered whoa: read the category descriptionb: Understood itThis is painting with light. Unfortunatly I think this (and a few others) will be hammered by non-photographers and photographers who misunderstand the photographic definition of painting with light. Well done.', '2004-01-26 23:23:35.000000', NULL, 1);
