(2022764, 55938, 656, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lhall:</b></div><hr/><i> Even after all this time, it''s hard for me NOT to come back to this to look at it.  So simple yet so very compelling to me - the movement of the image combined with the gaussian blur make it a continuing favorite of mine. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks - but there wasn''t any gaussian blur used in this shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by lhall: Even after all this time, it''s hard for me NOT to come back to this to look at it.  So simple yet so very compelling to me - the movement of the image combined with the gaussian blur make it a continuing favorite of mine.   Thanks - but there wasn''t any gaussian blur used in this shot.', '2006-01-10 17:58:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2097899, 55938, 13547, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Gordon:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lhall:</b></div><hr/><i> Even after all this time, it''s hard for me NOT to come back to this to look at it.  So simple yet so very compelling to me - the movement of the image combined with the gaussian blur make it a continuing favorite of mine. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks - but there wasn''t any gaussian blur used in this shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>But you said there was: "...Bit of selective gaussian blur..."</td>', 'Originally posted by Gordon: Originally posted by lhall: Even after all this time, it''s hard for me NOT to come back to this to look at it.  So simple yet so very compelling to me - the movement of the image combined with the gaussian blur make it a continuing favorite of mine.   Thanks - but there wasn''t any gaussian blur used in this shot.   But you said there was: "...Bit of selective gaussian blur..."', '2006-01-29 09:16:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2116579, 55938, 656, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by reevey:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Gordon:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lhall:</b></div><hr/><i> Even after all this time, it''s hard for me NOT to come back to this to look at it.  So simple yet so very compelling to me - the movement of the image combined with the gaussian blur make it a continuing favorite of mine. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks - but there wasn''t any gaussian blur used in this shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>But you said there was: "...Bit of selective gaussian blur..." </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>A true enough, but it was only on the small 1 cm diameter spot immediately above the bristles - probably not where you think it is.</td>', 'Originally posted by reevey: Originally posted by Gordon: Originally posted by lhall: Even after all this time, it''s hard for me NOT to come back to this to look at it.  So simple yet so very compelling to me - the movement of the image combined with the gaussian blur make it a continuing favorite of mine.   Thanks - but there wasn''t any gaussian blur used in this shot.   But you said there was: "...Bit of selective gaussian blur..."   A true enough, but it was only on the small 1 cm diameter spot immediately above the bristles - probably not where you think it is.', '2006-02-02 23:48:58.000000', NULL, 0),
